{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe nurse reviews a commercial driver's symptoms alongside information from a witness, the treating team and an older workplace form, because each source describes a different part of the story; the occupational record retains those differences and identifies completed current findings without turning a booking, a family account or a recollection into a measured patient result.\n\nThe driver's father required treatment for high blood pressure and a brother recently had a stroke, but the driver is describing their histories rather than his own diagnosis; he recalls a high pharmacy-machine number after a night shift without knowing the value, no current repeated blood-pressure series is available, and headaches attributed to noise and poor sleep have not been linked to a documented persistent pressure measurement.\n\nThe employer's copied form relates to an earlier period of work and contains a broad satisfactory box without the measurements underlying it, whereas the current nurse entry identifies the source of each specific finding; the driver's wish to continue scheduled duties is recorded as a preference, not as proof that the present assessment has resolved the documented concern.\n\nThe nurse keeps the relevant current attachment with the record and identifies the older account by its timing, so a later reviewer can distinguish what was observed, what the driver reported and what remains unresolved; no additional measurement, specialist conclusion or diagnosis is added merely because it would make the occupational decision easier to complete.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
